; The always-loaded Logo library (LOGO.md 5.4): the manual's "(library procedure)" entries that are not worth a JS
; primitive. Written from the manual's descriptions, NOT from the reference's logolib (decision 10).
; Everything here is marked a library procedure: PROCEDURES does not list it and ERALL leaves it alone.
; Iteration tools that must honour STOP / OUTPUT through their templates (MAP, FOREACH, FOR, ...) are machine operations in
; control.js, not definitions here.

; MDARRAY sizelist [origin]: an array of arrays, one level per size.
to mdarray :sizes [:origin 1]
localmake "result (array first :sizes :origin)
if emptyp bf :sizes [output :result]
for [i :origin [:origin + (first :sizes) - 1]] [setitem :i :result (mdarray bf :sizes :origin)]
output :result
end

; MDITEM indexlist array: follow one index per level.
to mditem :indexes :array
if emptyp :indexes [output :array]
output mditem bf :indexes (item first :indexes :array)
end

; MDSETITEM indexlist array value
to mdsetitem :indexes :array :value
if emptyp bf :indexes [setitem first :indexes :array :value stop]
mdsetitem bf :indexes (item first :indexes :array) :value
end
